ndex.ts`. Direct API match.\n\n## Runtime/framework mismatches (why so much is DOMAIN-ONLY)\n\nReading actual source (not just the README one-liners) surfaced stack facts the descriptions don't state:\n- **Bun runtime**, not Node (`Bun.********IDv7()`, `Bun.file()`) — llame pins Node ≥22.19.\n- **Elysia + TypeBox** backend (`t.Optional`, `t.UnionEnum`, `t.String`, `.get/.post/.put/.patch/.delete(path, handler)` route builder), not NestJS decorators.\n- **TanStack Router**, not Next.js App Router (`beforeLoad`, `loader`, `router.invalidate()`).\n- **better-result** (`TaggedError`, `panic()`) error model, not NestJS exceptions.\n- **Valkey/Redis** for coordination, not pg-boss-on-Postgres.\n- **Valibot**, not (confirmed) Zod, for schema validation.\n\nEach mismatch invalidates a cluster of rules wholesale (all TanStack-Router rules, all Elysia-route/TypeBox rules, all Valkey rules) even though the *underlying engineering concern* is often exactly something llame's own CLAUDE.md/CODING_STANDARDS/SPEC.md already states as policy.\n\n**One correction to my own README-based first pass**: `require-coordination-key`'s one-liner (\"declare the stable key for dedup/serialization\") reads like it could be pg-boss `singletonKey`. Reading the actual source shows it's entirely about Valkey **cluster hashtag placement** in `client.send(\"<COMMAND>\", [...])` calls — nothing to do with job dedup. DOMAIN-ONLY, not a pg-boss port candidate. Flagging because it's a case where the README alone would have misled a classification.\n\n## Bucket counts\n\n- **PORTABLE: 30**\n- **PORTABLE-WITH-WORK: 40**\n- **DOMAIN-ONLY: 61**\n- **NEEDS-TYPES: 0**\n\n## PORTABLE (30) — full source read, AST/scope-only, no type info, grounded against llame's actual code where noted\n\n| Rule | Detects | Mechanism | llame grounding |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `no-auth-token-in-web-storage` | credential-like keys written to `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` | scope-resolved (`getScope`) global-check + regex key heu